-### Parameters
-*   `fogDensity`: Default `0.005`. Raised from `0.0008` to ensure ~20% fog over 50 blocks and ~80% at the far plane, making the volume visible in the near/mid field [S1, unofficial].
-*   `farPlaneDistance`: Default `300`. Shortened to keep the volume visible in the near/mid field rather than only at the horizon [S1, unofficial].
-*   `phaseG`: Henyey-Greenstein phase function asymmetry parameter [S1, unofficial].
-*   `heightFalloff`: Controls density decay with height [S1, unofficial].
-
 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Type Mismatch:** The Beer-Lambert segment integral returns a `float3` (RGB). Declaring the accumulator as `float` causes compilation errors (e.g., E30019 in Slang) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Flat Appearance:** Using a large isotropic constant for ambient lighting washes out directional sun scattering. This is solved by sampling the sky-view LUT (`skyDome`) instead [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Low Visibility:** A default density of `0.0008` results in ~99.6% transparency at a few blocks, making fog invisible up close. Increasing to `0.005` fixes this [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Type Mismatch**: The Beer-Lambert segment integral returns a `float3` (RGB). The accumulator variable must be declared as `float3`, not `float`, to avoid compilation errors (e.g., E30019 in Slang) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Flat Appearance**: Using a huge isotropic constant for ambient lighting washes out directional sun scattering and flattens the volume. This is solved by sampling the sky-view LUT [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Low Visibility**: A default density of $0.0008$ per block results in ~99.6% transparency at a few blocks, making fog only visible as a faint distant band. Raising the density to $0.005$ and shortening the far plane to $300$ ensures ~20% fog over 50 blocks and ~80% at the far plane, making the volume clearly visible in the near/mid field [S1, unofficial].
 
